00:09:20.119 --> 00:09:22.939
So the alcohol, let's write
that down for ourselves so we

00:09:22.939 --> 00:09:24.319
can make notes for ourselves.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.790
The alcohol went from what to what?

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:32.650
So if I go back to my original
structure, So let's follow the alcohol.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:36.720
So we see, we have the OH
here now in the new structure.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.220
We see that it changed to this ether here.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.580
So it went from an alcohol to an ether.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.230
Now let's see, did it do anything
in the, in the next step?

00:09:45.349 --> 00:09:45.819
Well.

00:09:46.555 --> 00:09:51.045
In the second step, well, let's see,
we still have an ether and it remains

00:09:51.045 --> 00:09:52.585
the same, so it doesn't change.

00:09:52.585 --> 00:09:54.495
So there's no, it only has to change once.

00:09:54.815 --> 00:09:57.854
So that first step of the reaction
is really the hardest part.

00:09:58.255 --> 00:10:01.935
So, but however, we can break it
down for ourselves as seeing that.

00:10:01.965 --> 00:10:06.774
All right, well, this went from
an ether or alcohol to an ether.

00:10:07.294 --> 00:10:10.715
And then in step two, there was no change.

00:10:10.715 --> 00:10:13.305
So why don't we label that as
