00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:25.910
So, in summary, this alcohol
was added to this carbonyl, and

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.300
eventually we made a hemiacetal.

00:10:28.939 --> 00:10:31.369
We'll say hemis, because
that's our halfway point.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:38.900
So our acetal, and then it went
to a full blown acetal in the end.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.990
Now, just as a reminder, even though
I did not show it, a ketone can also

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.449
go through this reaction as well.

00:10:46.009 --> 00:10:50.409
And in that case, that would go from,
so if before it was an aldehyde.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:54.439
So if we have a ketone,
it'll turn into a hemiketal.

00:10:55.155 --> 00:11:00.425
So K E T A L, and eventually it'll
go through a same to its final step.

00:11:00.825 --> 00:11:02.615
Now, how can you tell the
difference between the two?

00:11:02.615 --> 00:11:06.035
Well, it's actually really
quite easy to do, is if you

00:11:06.035 --> 00:11:07.434
