00:11:12.285 --> 00:11:15.145
to, we see that there's a hydrogen here.

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:19.255
What is something that's on the aldehyde
structure in the very beginning?

00:11:19.805 --> 00:11:20.605
Well, go back.

00:11:20.944 --> 00:11:25.035
If you look at an aldehyde, notice
how it had its hydrogen here.

00:11:25.485 --> 00:11:30.005
So if you see a hydrogen at the very end,
that's how you can tell it's an acetal.

00:11:30.564 --> 00:11:33.114
Versus if it's a ketone,
